sequenceDiagram
    participant T as Thread TID 1001
    participant K as Linux scheduler/perf
    participant P2 as CPU 2 PMU
    participant P5 as CPU 5 PMU
    participant B as Perf ring buffer

    K->>P2: Schedule TID 1001 and restore event
    T->>P2: Run on CPU 2 and count events
    K->>P2: Switch out and account partial count
    Note over K: Logical TID event retains accumulated state
    K->>P5: Migrate TID 1001 and restore event
    T->>P5: Run on CPU 5 and continue logical count
    P5-->>K: Sampling threshold reached and interrupt CPU 5
    K->>B: Record sample with PID, TID 1001, CPU 5, IP, and call-chain data
    K->>P5: Reload the next sampling period
